==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|ham||in informal writing}}
* {{alter|de|han||archaic|dialectal}}

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|haben}}, from {{inh|de|goh|habēn}} (akin to {{cog|osx|hebbian}}, {{cog|non|hafa}} ({{cog|sv|hava}}/{{m|sv|ha}}), {{cog|ofs|habba}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽}}, {{cog|ang|habban}}), from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*habbjan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*habjaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||to grasp}}. Cognates include {{cog|bar|håbn}}, {{cog|yi|האָבן}}, {{cog|nl|hebben}}, {{cog|en|have}}, {{cog|da|have}}.

